You are a senior frontend engineer.

Context:
- Frontend application consumes backend APIs
- Backend APIs are documented using Swagger / OpenAPI
- Swagger is the SINGLE source of truth
- Swagger has been recently updated

Task:
Review the latest Swagger / OpenAPI documentation
and apply ALL required changes to the frontend so it fully matches Swagger.

Url: http://localhost:3000/api
Scope:
- Request payloads
- Query parameters
- Path parameters
- Response structures
- Status codes
- Required vs optional fields

Rules:
- Do NOT assume old API behavior
- Do NOT rely on previous frontend implementation
- Follow Swagger exactly as documented
- Update API calls, types/interfaces, and validations accordingly

Requirements:
- Update API service layer
- Update types/interfaces (TypeScript if used)
- Update forms and validations to match Swagger
- Handle new/changed error responses properly
- Ensure backward compatibility only if Swagger explicitly supports it

Constraints:
- Do NOT change backend code
- Do NOT modify Swagger
- Frontend changes only

Validation:
- No API call should send undocumented fields
- All required fields must be sent
- Frontend correctly handles all documented responses
- No console errors related to API mismatch

Output:
- List Swagger changes detected
- Show frontend files updated
- Explain how frontend now aligns with Swagger
